PUBLIC BRIEF: {"buyer":"Southeast Louisiana Legal Services","exclusions":["Experimental guardrail: no employee compensation decisions, salary changes, HR-system access or implementation of benefits/classification changes is authorized.","Full job descriptions, authorized compensation/benefit records, market datasets and the referenced salary-scale attachment were not obtained as usable inputs; actual analysis and final recommendations remain input-dependent.","Historical milestones are preserved as source facts, not newly assigned deadlines. No target salary, fee ceiling or quantified pay/benefit change is invented."],"id":"slls-compensation-analysis-2023","requirements":[{"brick":"correlate","id":"R1","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Analyze market salaries for all SLLS positions, comparing relevant local nonprofit and government employers."},{"brick":"review","id":"R2","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Review job descriptions with SLLS and recommend longevity incentives, including possible new staff classifications; the stated longevity stage target is June 30, 2024."},{"brick":"draft","id":"R3","owner":"human_required","text":"Recommend position and compensation changes based on the analysis; the stated salary-scale recommendation target is November 15, 2023."},{"brick":"correlate","id":"R4","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Conduct a comparable-market review of health insurance, retirement, time off and other benefits; the stated benefits-review target is March 31, 2024."},{"brick":"draft","id":"R5","owner":"human_required","text":"Recommend appropriate changes to the benefits package."},{"brick":"draft","id":"R6","owner":"human_required","text":"Recommend changes to annual salary-step levels; the stated step-recommendation target is December 31, 2023."},{"brick":"report","id":"R7","owner":"blocked_private_input","text":"Deliver a final report to the SLLS Personnel Committee covering completed research, the process, recommendations and their rationale."}],"source_url":"https://slls.org/en/salary-study-rfp/","summary":"Historical 2023 RFP for a compensation analysis with SLLS management and its Board Personnel Committee. Work covers salaries, job classifications and longevity incentives, benefits, annual step increases and a final justified report, using local nonprofit/government comparisons and supporting competitiveness and DEI. Staged targets run from November 2023 through June 2024; the notice is not current.","title":"Request for Proposals: Compensation Analysis"}
